@@ -29,8 +29,15 @@ mozva stub around `widget/gtk` `va_drmcommon.h`; `drmGetDevice` comes from
 
 All source files match their path from the library's source archive.
 
-Currently, we only use the vp8, vp9, av1 (via libdav1d), mp3, flac, vorbis (via
-libvorbis), opus (via libopus) and PCM portion of the library. If this changes,
+Currently, we only use the vp8, vp9, av1 (via libdav1d), h264, hevc, aac, mp3,
+flac, vorbis (via libvorbis), opus (via libopus) and PCM portion of the library.
+The h264, hevc and aac decoders and parsers come with the sources that FFmpeg
+9.0.1's `configure --enable-decoder=h264,hevc,aac --enable-parser=h264,hevc,aac`
+selects on top of `FFMPEG_CONFIGURATION`; the subsystems they need are switched
+on in `config_override.h`. H.264 and HEVC are wired with their x86 DSP only
+and stay off on other CPUs. AAC, with the float `libavutil/tx` transforms and
+float DSP it uses, runs plain C only (`aac-c-only.patch`), so its output does
+not depend on the CPU. If this changes,
 configuration files will most likely need to be updated. On Windows,
 we use d3d11va for vp9 and av1.
 
@@ -222,3 +229,39 @@ Finally, apply the patches:
   nasm cannot parse a relational operator inside parentheses until 2.15, and
   our minimum supported nasm (used by the base-toolchains builds) is 2.14.02.
   Drop this patch once that minimum is raised past 2.15.
+- In `aacdec_proc_template.c`, call `cbrt` (fdlibm through
+  modules/fdlibm/inexact-math-override) instead of `cbrtf`: the override maps `cbrtf` to `fdlibm_cbrtf`, which
+  fdlibm does not have. The double result rounds to the same float.
+- libavutil/md5.c, ambient_viewing_environment.c and tdrdi.c (with their
+  headers, already in the tree) are copied unchanged from FFmpeg n9.0.1
+  (commit bf1b838f2ab88b4f8fd83443325c782ea0e0f7fa), line endings aside. The
+  H.264 and HEVC SEI code needs them.
+- AAC runs plain C whatever the CPU: `AV_TX_FFVPX_C_ONLY` (tx.h, tx.c) makes
+  av_tx_init pick only C codelets, `AV_FLOAT_DSP_FFVPX_C_ONLY` (float_dsp.h/.c)
+  makes avpriv_float_dsp_alloc return the C functions, and aacdec.c,
+  aacdec_float.c and aacsbr_template.c ask for them. The x86 inits of the AAC
+  SBR and PS DSP are off by `MOZ_FFVPX_AAC_C_ONLY` (config_override.h).
+- The AAC-LC float decoder gives the samples of Media Foundation (Windows 11,
+  msauddecmft.dll 10.0.26100.9549), bit for bit, on every OS and CPU. The logic
+  is the FFmpeg 6.1.1 patch of invisible_MediaFoundation
+  (reimpl/ffmpeg/ffmpeg-6.1.1-mf.patch) moved to the 9.0.1 layout:
+  - libavcodec/aac/aacdec_mf.h (new, included by aacdec_float.c): scalefactor
+    to gain (ExponentTableFl), x^(4/3) for |q| >= 1024 and pulses, the TNS
+    lattice filter, PNS (generator, gain, correlated noise with M/S), and the
+    IMDCT with its windows. The AVX2/FMA path of the DLL is a constant, the host
+    CPU is never read.
+  - libavcodec/aac/mf_dct.[ch], mf_imlt.[ch] (new): the DLL's dct_IV and
+    imlt_block in portable C. mf_tables.[ch] (new): the DLL's float tables as
+    bit patterns (sine and KBD windows, twiddles, 2^(k/4), TNS coefficients),
+    read from its .rdata by scripts/gen_tables.py.
+  - aacdec.c: PNS energy kept as the DLL clamps it (sce->mf_pns_nrg), TNS
+    coefficients from the DLL's tables, PNS applied after M/S and intensity
+    stereo (also for SCE), IMDCT state reset in flush.
+  - aacdec_dsp_template.c: scalefactors by mf_sf2exp, M/S on every band with
+    the bit set, TNS by the lattice filter, IMDCT for AOT_AAC_LC.
+  - aacdec_proc_template.c: PNS bands are left to mf_apply_pns, escape values
+    >= 1024 and pulses dequantized as the DLL does, pulses in zero bands.
+  - moz.build: the new sources, and -ffp-contract=off on them and on
+    aacdec_float.c (the sign of zero and every rounding are part of the output).
+  Not ported: SBR and PS (HE-AAC) still decode with FFmpeg's code, and the
+  concealment of streams the DLL rejects.
